<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">autoskill</ansi>

Some of your company's skills work automatically, so you don't have to
call for them every time. Whoever in your company is best at a given one
handles it - you or a companion, whichever has the higher level in it.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What runs automatically</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">traps</ansi>   sensing traps as you walk into a room, and once, for
           free, the moment you start picking a trapped lock
           (<ansi fg="command">help trap</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="yellow">light</ansi>   conjuring a floating light when you step into the
           dark and nobody in your company is already carrying one
  <ansi fg="yellow">trail</ansi>   reading the trail beyond the exits as you walk
           (<ansi fg="command">help trail</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="yellow">pathfinder</ansi>  easing rough ground (<ansi fg="command">help pathfinder</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="yellow">keeneye</ansi> spotting secret exits (<ansi fg="command">help keeneye</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="yellow">weather</ansi> the forecast in <ansi fg="command">weather</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help forecast</ansi>)
  <ansi fg="yellow">haggle</ansi>  better market prices (<ansi fg="command">help haggle</ansi>)

A companion who is down is never considered. For a light, a companion
who is fighting or out of mana is passed over too, so a busy companion
never blocks an able one from stepping in.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">autoskill</ansi>
  Show each automatic skill and whether it's on or off for you.

  <ansi fg="command">autoskill [skill] on</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">autoskill [skill] off</ansi>
  Turn one on or off. All are on by default.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trap</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help light</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help picklock</ansi>.